  "allsearch_version": "0.3.0",
  "provider_query": "Which organization does the CVE program identify as the source of CVE records used by NVD",
  "answer": "The CVE Program identifies the **CVE List** (the official catalog of CVE Records) as what feeds the NVD. That list is produced by the **CVE Program**, operated by **The MITRE Corporation** (with CISA sponsorship). NVD (NIST) is a separate program that ingests those records and enriches them.\n\nRelevant sources:\n\n1. **CVE.org – Related Efforts** — CVE and NVD are separate. The CVE List, launched by The MITRE Corporation in 1999, “feeds NVD,” which builds on information in CVE Records.  \n   https://www.cve.org/about/relatedefforts\n\n2. **CVE.org – FAQs** — Same relationship: the CVE List feeds NVD; CVE Records are used by NVD and other products. MITRE (via the HSSEDI FFRDC) operates the CVE Program Secretariat.  \n   https://www.cve.org/ResourcesSupport/FAQs\n\n3. **NVD – CVE FAQs** — NVD enriches each CVE after it is published to the CVE List (descriptions, references, then NVD tags, CVSS, CWE, CPE).  \n   https://nvd.nist.gov/general/FAQ-Sections/CVE-FAQs\n\n4. **NVD – CVEs and the NVD Process** — The CVE program is maintained by MITRE (sponsored by DHS/CISA). CVEs published to the CVE List typically appear in NVD within about an hour; NVD then enriches them.  \n   https://nvd.nist.gov/general/cve-process\n\n5. **NVD – Developers** — The CVE Program is maintained by MITRE; NVD analyzes each CVE after publication to the CVE List.  \n   https://nvd.nist.gov/developers\n\n6. **CVE List V5 (GitHub, CVEProject/cvelistV5)** — Official CVE List of records identified by or reported to the CVE Program; updated from the CVE Services API. This is the program’s bulk source of CVE Records.  \n   https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5\n\n7. **CVE.org – Process** — CVE Records are the descriptive data for a CVE ID, provided by CNA partners and published to the CVE List (the public source NVD consumes).  \n   https://www.cve.org/About/Process\n\n8. **NVD CVE API schema notes** — NVD records include a `sourceIdentifier` for the CNA that assigned the CVE; the underlying CVE content still originates from the CVE List, not from NVD.  \n   https://nvd.nist.gov/developers/vulnerabilities",
